# AEGIS typed contracts & ports

Follow `Docs/specs/Engineering/TYPED_CONTRACTS_PORTS_FASTAPI.md` and `Docs/specs/Engineering/OPENTELEMETRY_TELEMETRY.md`.

- Type-hint all public APIs.
- Use Pydantic v2 with `strict=True` and `extra="forbid"` for API, LLM, tool, and workflow contracts.
- Validate tool/function-calling args before execution; return typed error models.
- Keep domain free of FastAPI/Neo4j/OTel SDK imports — use ports & adapters.
- FastAPI routers only parse, call services, and map errors; expose OpenAPI `/docs`.
- Typed HTTP clients: retries with exponential backoff + jitter; bounded attempts.
- Instrument with OpenTelemetry via `TelemetryPort`; default offline console/file exporter.
- Never put secrets, raw PV narratives, or system prompts into OTel attributes.
- CLI/eval must work offline without React or Neo4j (use graph stub).
- Work only under `submission/`; do not modify challenge evidence.
